From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aire-One <aireone@aireone.xyz>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 00:37:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix build and runtime with Lua 5.5

Lua 5.5 makes for-loop control variables read-only, so assigning to
them is now a compile error. In 4.3 this breaks loading the fair
layout (and so rc.lua) and the docs build.

Backported from upstream commit 05b8695d0433
("chore: support build and tests for Lua 5.5"), only the parts that
apply to 4.3.
---
 docs/ldoc.ltp                  | 6 +++---
 lib/awful/layout/suit/fair.lua | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/ldoc.ltp b/docs/ldoc.ltp
index f7a7501..d270f1e 100644
--- a/docs/ldoc.ltp
+++ b/docs/ldoc.ltp
@@ -289,9 +289,9 @@
   <p>$(M(ldoc.full_description,nil))</p>
 # end
 
-# for kind, mods in ldoc.kinds() do
-<h2>$(kind)</h2>
-# kind = kind:lower()
+# for k, mods in ldoc.kinds() do
+<h2>$(k)</h2>
+# kind = k:lower()
 <table class="module_list">
 # for m in mods() do
 	<tr>
diff --git a/lib/awful/layout/suit/fair.lua b/lib/awful/layout/suit/fair.lua
index 161b6ed..1a97cb9 100644
--- a/lib/awful/layout/suit/fair.lua
+++ b/lib/awful/layout/suit/fair.lua
@@ -41,8 +41,8 @@ local function do_fair(p, orientation)
             cols = math.ceil(#cls / rows)
         end
 
-        for k, c in ipairs(cls) do
-            k = k - 1
+        for i, c in ipairs(cls) do
+            local k = i - 1
             local g = {}
 
             local row, col
